data: {"type": "insight", "data": {"executive_summary": "1,500 dock appointments across three facilities over 5 months show a 72.0% on-time arrival rate and an average dwell of 2.32 hours, with Columbus DC standing out for notably longer dwell times. The dataset covers 1,500 appointments from June through November 2026 across Dallas Cross-Dock, Reno DC, and Columbus DC, tracking dwell time, on-time arrival, and no-shows. Columbus DC's average dwell is well above the other two facilities, and one record contains an extreme dwell value that inflates the overall average.", "technical_findings": ["Loaded 1,500 rows \u00d7 12 columns from a JSON file. (n = 1,500; high confidence: Read as-is: no layout guessing was needed.)", "dwell_hours MoM: -1.7% (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "Appointment ID MoM: -98.7% (n = 1,500; high confidence: 1500 rows)", "hours_before_appointment MoM: -51.9% (n = 979; high confidence: 979 rows)", "avg_dwell_hours (from dwell_hours) by Facility (1 groups) (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "on_time_arrival (from hours_before_appointment) by Facility (1 groups) (n = 979; high confidence: 979 rows)", "visits_over_2h (from dwell_hours) by Facility (1 groups) (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "count Appointment ID by Status (1 groups) (n = 1,500; high confidence: 1500 rows)", "count Appointment ID by Facility (1 groups) (n = 1,500; high confidence: 1500 rows)", "avg_dwell_hours (from dwell_hours) by Facility (3 groups) (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "on_time_arrival (from hours_before_appointment) by Facility (3 groups) (n = 979; high confidence: 979 rows)", "count Appointment ID by Facility (3 groups) (n = 1,500; high confidence: 1500 rows)", "avg_dwell_hours (from dwell_hours) by Carrier (5 groups) (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "on_time_arrival (from hours_before_appointment) by Carrier (5 groups) (n = 979; high confidence: 979 rows)", "count Appointment ID by Carrier (5 groups) (n = 1,500; high confidence: 1500 rows)", "avg_dwell_hours (from dwell_hours) by Direction (2 groups) (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "on_time_arrival (from hours_before_appointment) by Direction (2 groups) (n = 979; high confidence: 979 rows)", "count Appointment ID by Direction (2 groups) (n = 1,500; high confidence: 1500 rows)", "1 unusual values in dwell_hours (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "dwell_hours: median 1.60, mean 2.32, range 0.06667 to 612.60 (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "hours_before_appointment: median 0.3333, mean 0.3713, range 0 to 1.55 (n = 979; high confidence: 979 rows)", "hours_late_to_appointment: median 0.1833, mean 0.229, range 0 to 0.9833 (n = 403; high confidence: 403 rows)"], "recommended_actions": [{"priority": 1, "action": "Investigate and resolve the single appointment record showing 612.60 hours of dwell before using the average dwell figure in any reporting or target-setting.", "reasoning": "Removes a value that distorts the overall average for all 1,356 dwell rows.", "metric_impact": "Removes a value that distorts the overall average for all 1,356 dwell rows."}, {"priority": 2, "action": "Review dock scheduling and turnaround processes at Columbus DC to understand why average dwell is more than double that of the other two facilities.", "reasoning": "Columbus DC accounts for 360 visits; reducing dwell there would improve network-wide throughput.", "metric_impact": "Columbus DC accounts for 360 visits; reducing dwell there would improve network-wide throughput."}, {"priority": 3, "action": "Investigate on-time arrival at Dallas Cross-Dock, which has the lowest rate among the three facilities, to identify whether scheduling, carrier mix, or lane patterns are associated with late arrivals.", "reasoning": "Improving on-time arrival reduces dock idle time and downstream delays.", "metric_impact": "Improving on-time arrival reduces dock idle time and downstream delays."}], "anomaly_alerts": [{"title": "How these numbers are counted", "severity": "low", "description": "Read as logistics data (average dwell, on-time arrival, visits over 2 h at the dock, no-shows, dock appointments). Rates pool their parts (on-time, OTIF, fill and cost per lb are totals divided, never averages of per-shipment rates). On time means on or before the promised date, dates as written (local); an early delivery is on time. Transit is in calendar days from the ship date. Cost is in the main currency only. Nov 2026 is partial (data through the 1st) and is left out of period comparisons. 38 cancelled rows are left out of every count and rate. The data covers 5 months, so month-over-month changes may be seasonal (a peak season); there is no same month last year to compare with. Drivers are people: figures by driver describe the visits, never rank the people, and groups of fewer than 11 drivers are not shown. A carrier's figures depend on its lanes, modes and shippers: a difference between carriers is an association, not the carrier's doing, and every rate is given with its number of shipments.", "affected_metric": "", "suggested_investigation": ""}], "proactive_questions": ["What operational or process differences at Columbus DC explain its average dwell being more than twice that of Dallas Cross-Dock?", "Is the 612.60-hour dwell record a data entry error, a genuine exception (e.g., a held shipment), or a system timestamp issue?", "Do the 103 no-shows concentrate at a particular facility, carrier, or time of week, and what is their impact on dock utilization?"], "methodology_notes": "Cleaning (cleaning rules-v1): Final dataset: 1500 rows (started with 1500). Analysis (analysis v9) computed: anomaly, eda, segment, source, trend. Descriptive statistics use the non-missing values of each column. Month-over-month compares calendar-month totals (means for rates and 0-1 flags).", "executive_view": {"headline": "1,500 dock appointments across three facilities over 5 months show a 72.0% on-time arrival rate and an average dwell of 2.32 hours, with Columbus DC standing out for notably longer dwell times.", "headline_evidence_ids": ["source:data", "seg:Facility/dwell_hours:ratio:avg_dwell_hours", "seg:Facility/hours_before_appointment:ratio:on_time_arrival"], "paragraphs": [{"text": "The dataset covers 1,500 appointments from June through November 2026 across Dallas Cross-Dock, Reno DC, and Columbus DC, tracking dwell time, on-time arrival, and no-shows.", "evidence_ids": ["source:data", "clean:audit"], "typed": null}, {"text": "Columbus DC's average dwell is well above the other two facilities, and one record contains an extreme dwell value that inflates the overall average.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Facility/dwell_hours:ratio:avg_dwell_hours", "anom:dwell_hours"], "typed": null}], "findings": [{"text": "Columbus DC averages 4.48 hours of dwell per visit, compared with 1.89 hours at Reno DC and 1.39 hours at Dallas Cross-Dock.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Facility/dwell_hours:ratio:avg_dwell_hours"], "typed": null}, {"text": "On-time arrival is 76.6% at Columbus DC, 72.1% at Reno DC, and 69.3% at Dallas Cross-Dock; the overall rate is 72.0%.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Facility/hours_before_appointment:ratio:on_time_arrival"], "typed": null}, {"text": "One appointment record shows a dwell of 612.60 hours, far outside the expected range, and will inflate any average that includes it.", "evidence_ids": ["anom:dwell_hours", "eda:dwell_hours"], "typed": null}, {"text": "Outbound visits average 2.78 hours of dwell while inbound visits average 1.83 hours; visit counts are nearly balanced at 743 outbound and 719 inbound.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Direction/dwell_hours:ratio:avg_dwell_hours", "seg:Direction/Appointment ID:count"], "typed": null}, {"text": "Avg dwell hours: Columbus DC (4.48) is higher than Dallas Cross-Dock (1.39).", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Facility/dwell_hours:ratio:avg_dwell_hours"], "typed": {"kind": "comparison", "evidence_id": "seg:Facility/dwell_hours:ratio:avg_dwell_hours", "cause": "", "effect": "", "metric": "avg_dwell_hours", "verdict": "", "source": "", "a": "Columbus DC", "b": "Dallas Cross-Dock"}}, {"text": "Avg dwell hours: Outbound (2.78) is higher than Inbound (1.83).", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Direction/dwell_hours:ratio:avg_dwell_hours"], "typed": {"kind": "comparison", "evidence_id": "seg:Direction/dwell_hours:ratio:avg_dwell_hours", "cause": "", "effect": "", "metric": "avg_dwell_hours", "verdict": "", "source": "", "a": "Outbound", "b": "Inbound"}}], "action_items": [{"action": "Investigate and resolve the single appointment record showing 612.60 hours of dwell before using the average dwell figure in any reporting or target-setting.", "expected_impact": "Removes a value that distorts the overall average for all 1,356 dwell rows.", "evidence_ids": ["anom:dwell_hours", "eda:dwell_hours"]}, {"action": "Review dock scheduling and turnaround processes at Columbus DC to understand why average dwell is more than double that of the other two facilities.", "expected_impact": "Columbus DC accounts for 360 visits; reducing dwell there would improve network-wide throughput.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Facility/dwell_hours:ratio:avg_dwell_hours", "seg:Facility/Appointment ID:count"]}, {"action": "Investigate on-time arrival at Dallas Cross-Dock, which has the lowest rate among the three facilities, to identify whether scheduling, carrier mix, or lane patterns are associated with late arrivals.", "expected_impact": "Improving on-time arrival reduces dock idle time and downstream delays.", "evidence_ids": ["seg:Facility/hours_before_appointment:ratio:on_time_arrival", "seg:Carrier/hours_before_appointment:ratio:on_time_arrival"]}]}, "analyst_view": {"methodology": "Cleaning (cleaning rules-v1): Final dataset: 1500 rows (started with 1500). Analysis (analysis v9) computed: anomaly, eda, segment, source, trend. Descriptive statistics use the non-missing values of each column. Month-over-month compares calendar-month totals (means for rates and 0-1 flags).", "statistical_notes": ["Loaded 1,500 rows \u00d7 12 columns from a JSON file. (n = 1,500; high confidence: Read as-is: no layout guessing was needed.)", "dwell_hours MoM: -1.7% (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "Appointment ID MoM: -98.7% (n = 1,500; high confidence: 1500 rows)", "hours_before_appointment MoM: -51.9% (n = 979; high confidence: 979 rows)", "avg_dwell_hours (from dwell_hours) by Facility (1 groups) (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "on_time_arrival (from hours_before_appointment) by Facility (1 groups) (n = 979; high confidence: 979 rows)", "visits_over_2h (from dwell_hours) by Facility (1 groups) (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "count Appointment ID by Status (1 groups) (n = 1,500; high confidence: 1500 rows)", "count Appointment ID by Facility (1 groups) (n = 1,500; high confidence: 1500 rows)", "avg_dwell_hours (from dwell_hours) by Facility (3 groups) (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "on_time_arrival (from hours_before_appointment) by Facility (3 groups) (n = 979; high confidence: 979 rows)", "count Appointment ID by Facility (3 groups) (n = 1,500; high confidence: 1500 rows)", "avg_dwell_hours (from dwell_hours) by Carrier (5 groups) (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "on_time_arrival (from hours_before_appointment) by Carrier (5 groups) (n = 979; high confidence: 979 rows)", "count Appointment ID by Carrier (5 groups) (n = 1,500; high confidence: 1500 rows)", "avg_dwell_hours (from dwell_hours) by Direction (2 groups) (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "on_time_arrival (from hours_before_appointment) by Direction (2 groups) (n = 979; high confidence: 979 rows)", "count Appointment ID by Direction (2 groups) (n = 1,500; high confidence: 1500 rows)", "1 unusual values in dwell_hours (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "dwell_hours: median 1.60, mean 2.32, range 0.06667 to 612.60 (n = 1,356; high confidence: 1356 rows)", "hours_before_appointment: median 0.3333, mean 0.3713, range 0 to 1.55 (n = 979; high confidence: 979 rows)", "hours_late_to_appointment: median 0.1833, mean 0.229, range 0 to 0.9833 (n = 403; high confidence: 403 rows)"], "caveats": ["38 cancelled appointments are excluded from all counts and rates; their inclusion could change volume and on-time figures.", "November 2026 is partial (data through the 1st only) and is excluded from month-over-month comparisons; the 5-month window is too short to distinguish trends from seasonality.", "The extreme dwell record (612.60 hours) is included in the overall mean of 2.32 hours; the median of 1.60 hours is a more representative central value until that record is resolved.", "Read as logistics data (average dwell, on-time arrival, visits over 2 h at the dock, no-shows, dock appointments). Rates pool their parts (on-time, OTIF, fill and cost per lb are totals divided, never averages of per-shipment rates). On time means on or before the promised date, dates as written (local); an early delivery is on time. Transit is in calendar days from the ship date. Cost is in the main currency only.", "Nov 2026 is partial (data through the 1st) and is left out of period comparisons.", "38 cancelled rows are left out of every count and rate.", "The data covers 5 months, so month-over-month changes may be seasonal (a peak season); there is no same month last year to compare with.", "Drivers are people: figures by driver describe the visits, never rank the people, and groups of fewer than 11 drivers are not shown.", "A carrier's figures depend on its lanes, modes and shippers: a difference between carriers is an association, not the carrier's doing, and every rate is given with its number of shipments.", "2 columns hold personal data; their values are masked before any model sees them.", "Arrived At: Filled only for rows whose status needs it, so other rows are blank by design; 0% of those rows have no value. Kept as it is.", "Departed At: Filled only for rows whose status needs it, so other rows are blank by design; 0% of those rows have no value. Kept as it is."], "code_references": ["df['Facility'].value_counts()"]}, "additional_issues_note": "", "generated_at": "2026-11-18 17:54:03.719382+00:00", "memory_used": []}}

